From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:13:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec: DRM PRIME frames, AV1 and P010

The decoders offer their frames as AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME beside the
software format, and get_format picks: each capture buffer's planes are
exported once as dma-bufs (VIDIOC_EXPBUF) and described in an
AVDRMFrameDescriptor that lives with the buffer. The frame's buf[0]
returns the buffer to the driver when released, as for software frames.
The default get_format keeps choosing the software format.

av1_v4l2m2m decodes AV1 where the driver offers V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1, and
P010 capture maps to AV_PIX_FMT_P010 and DRM_FORMAT_P010.

For the stateful decoders around them:
- a new capture pixel format at the same size, such as a 10-bit stream,
  reinitialises the capture queue as a new size does, and a capture
  queue the driver refuses before it has parsed the stream is set up
  again with the next packet;
- after a source change the visible size comes from G_SELECTION where
  the driver has it, not from the buffers' padded size;
- an empty capture buffer marked as an error (Iris returns one for each
  frame the stream decodes but does not show) goes back to the driver
  instead of out as a frame;
- with neither pkt_timebase nor time_base set, as Firefox leaves them,
  timestamps pass through unchanged instead of being lost.
